  partName: Left Rear Intake Runner Bolt
  description: The Left Rear Intake Runner Bolt is a small, elongated bolt situated
    at the top-left-rear of the engine, constructed from Material.001, which fastens
    the intake runner to the engine block, enabling efficient airflow into the cylinders.
    This bolt plays a vital role in maintaining engine power and efficiency. Notably,
    its tiny size requires precise torque specification to avoid damage.
